n the six  you might have to kill the palace guards  are you okay with that and indeed there  was violence against the so-called  palace guards u.s capitol police there  to defend the capital another message  reported by the post stated in an  apparent reference to killing officers  drop a handful the rest will flee  meaning  kill a few u.s capitol police and then  they're going to get out of our way  on december 19 trump tweeted a message  exhorting his followers to come to dc on  january 6 writing quote big protest in  dc on january 6 be there will be wild  that lit up online pro-trump groups and  fbi informants quickly began passing on  information about highly specific  planning for a violent attack in  washington here's how the post puts it  the fbi received a call alerting them to  trump supporters making plans online to  bring arms to washington and arrest  lawmakers  that the sunday afternoon call was  handled by the bureau's national threat  operations center a clearinghouse for  tips about crimes according to a  document titled threats to take guns and  overrun the dc police january 4 to  january 20th  it's almost like the 911 memo bin laden  poised to strike  threats to take guns and overrun dc  police  the file was updated the following  afternoon by an fbi employee seeking to  reclassify the information more domestic  terrorism than criminal in nature they  wanted to say hey this is almost not  even just criminal this is domestic  terrorism criminal has received a number  of guardians as a significant number of  guardians as a result of threats to  congress and other government officials  the caller according to the fbi document  said people were planning on meeting in  certain areas  and sneaking guns into dc in an attempt  to overrun the dc police beginning  january 4th through 20th on three  different sites there is discussion  about recruitment where to meet at bring  guns and arresting senators and members  of congress to hold trials outside in  public areas in one specific threat utah  republican senator mitt romney often  regarded by trump supporters as a  traitor to magda  was named as a target  yet despite all of this on december 22nd  the post says the fbi  closed its internal threat assessment of  the matter determining it did not  warrant further investigation at this  time  an fbi official told the post that  before doing so steps were taken to  share the info but ultimately the  determination was made that the tips  they received featured vague and  primarily first amendment protected  speech  when we think back and we say  how were they not more ready  and why was the national guard not  deployed in advance and even as the  capital was being overrun  and as we follow the chain of command  upward we learned that on the day of  it was donald trump who was reportedly  gleefully watching the first couple of  hours of the riots maybe thinking it  would actually prevent joe biden from  ultimately being certified as president  of the united states  later trump started to not really like  that the rioters looked low class and  made him look bad  but the pressure was building for him to  deploy the national guard he was told  mike pence is potentially in danger mike  pence had to be evacuated they were  chanting hang mike pence but we know  that trump was actually mad at mike  pence trump was furious that pence  wasn't willing to do what trump believed  pence could do to really stop the  certification of joe biden as president  even though pence accurately told him i  can't do that sir i can't do that um and  the calls built for trump to call off  the protesters and to send in the  national guard and it was trump who  resisted doing that on january 6th but  this is a much broader backstory of a  sort of hot potato that was being played  behind the scenes the fbi  was at the time that they could say this  is criminal not domestic terrorism  sort of letting the dc police know you  might want to do something ab